# Trivy suppressions. One ID per line; Trivy applies them to every scanner
# (vulnerabilities, secrets, misconfigurations).
#
# Policy: a suppression is a temporary, reviewed risk acceptance, not a fix.
#   1. Put a comment directly above the entry: WHY it is safe/unfixable and a tracking issue.
#   2. Give it an expiry date with `exp:` so it resurfaces automatically.
#   3. Prefer fixing (upgrade the dependency, harden the manifest) over ignoring.
#
# Formats (https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#by-finding-ids):
#   CVE-2099-0001 exp:2099-01-31     # vulnerability, ignored until the date
#   AVD-KSV-0001  exp:2099-01-31     # misconfiguration check ID
#   generic-api-key                  # secret rule ID
#
# There are intentionally no active entries: the repository currently passes the gate cleanly.
